{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/vlpkhx","slideIndex":1,"text":"Chicago showed much greater temperature variation: a standard deviation of about 10.9 degrees Celsius, compared with 2.8 in San Diego. The marked highest daily means were about 28.3 degrees in Chicago and 24.6 in San Diego. These are maxima within this sample. That contrast led me to ask whether the same model settings would suit both cities.\n\nPlanned narration: 25 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: Notebook cell 60. Statistics describe daily mean temperatures in this two-year sample."}
