{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/4c3tng","slideIndex":2,"text":"I also examined wind on March thirteenth, 2010, the day with the largest displayed regional precipitation value. This was exploratory. The regional average covers a rectangle rather than a United States land mask, and the precipitation scaling still needs validation as daily rainfall totals. That uncertainty helped me narrow the final modeling focus to temperature.\n\nPlanned narration: 25 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: Notebook cell 61. Region means use the rectangular study area, without a country mask."}
