{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/347xbv","slideIndex":4,"text":"I then changed the question: can a neural network learn the seasonal temperature pattern from day of year alone? I trained on 2009 and evaluated on 2010. Chicago’s average absolute error fell from 8.91 degrees for straight-line regression to 2.92 for the network. San Diego’s fell from 1.68 to 1.48. The network could represent the seasonal rise and fall that a straight line missed. This evaluates a different task from predicting tomorrow’s weather.\n\nPlanned narration: 35 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: Saved notebook cell 64 results. Train on 2009, evaluate on 2010."}
