{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hpcb85","slideIndex":5,"text":"To choose network settings with coverage of every season, I held out the final seven days of each month in 2009. That gave 84 validation days and 281 training days. This asks how well the model fills gaps within one year, so its scores cannot be compared directly with the 2010 evaluation. I compared five, ten, and twenty neurons. Chicago’s lowest validation error was about 2.50 degrees with ten neurons. San Diego’s was about 1.18 with twenty. Better training fit did not consistently mean better validation predictions.\n\nPlanned narration: 40 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: month_end_results/model_comparison.csv. Same dates, preprocessing and seed for every width."}
