{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/shg0bb","slideIndex":6,"text":"Week Six suggested controlling overfitting with regularization. I varied the L2 penalty, which discourages large weights, while keeping network size fixed. The original models already used a weak penalty. For San Diego’s ten-neuron model, increasing alpha from 0.0001 to 0.001 reduced validation error from 1.28 to 1.21 degrees, about six percent. Training error rose slightly, from 1.15 to 1.19. This helped a smaller model, while the original overall MAE winners remained unchanged.\n\nPlanned narration: 35 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: week6_regularization_results/comparison.csv. San Diego, 10 neurons, same monthly split and seed."}
