{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/3hbxfu","slideIndex":8,"text":"I averaged five networks with different initial weights to test whether predictions became more reliable. The ensemble did not beat either city’s original winner. Some weaker fits pulled the mean away from better solutions. In the appendix plot, the shaded spread shows disagreement between fits. It is not a calibrated interval for future temperatures.\n\nPlanned narration: 25 seconds.\nThis slide belongs to the five-minute main presentation.\n\nSource: week6_ensemble_results/scores.csv. Five fixed seeds, 0 through 4, averaged in Celsius."}
